{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>When Rachel had borne Joseph.</b> Once the adversary of Esau was born — as it says, ״וְהָיָה בֵית יַעֲקֹב אֵשׁ וּבֵית יוֹסֵף לֶהָבָה וּבֵית עֵשָׂו לְקַשׁ״ (Obadiah 1) — fire without a flame has no dominion from afar. Once Joseph was born, Jacob trusted in the Holy One, blessed be He, and wanted to return."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:16.528283312Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}